    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Lawrence Butler** standing as our premier play (73.95). He carries the highest floor on the board, benefiting significantly from a favorable park factor and a 4.21 xERA matchup against Kumar Rocker. While **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also provides a strong start, his upside is bolstered by a massive 19% boost from facing Bassitt, whose 4.91 xERA suggests we should see plenty of baserunners in front of the middle of the order. **Gleyber Torres** (59.88) and **Brendan Donovan** (59.33) serve as our backbone for efficiency, with **Gleyber Torres** capitalizing on a prime lead-off spot against Newcomb, and **Brendan Donovan** enjoying a significant 14% platoon edge against Lambert. \n\nThe primary lineup risk today involves pending confirmations for **Zack Gelof** and **Jung Hoo Lee**; while we have modeled their scores based on projected #3 and #1 spots respectively, any downward move in their batting order will erode their efficiency. **Gavin Sheets** (40.12) barely cleared our threshold, as he is fighting against a brutal matchup with Williams (2.90 xERA), making him the most precarious start in the outfield. **Braden Montgomery** was our most difficult cut (39.17), falling just short of the 40.0 floor due to a poor matchup against Jobe; we opted to prioritize the platoon advantages of **JJ Bleday** and **Daulton Varsho** over the raw power profile of **Braden Montgomery** today to ensure we don't bleed points in the AVG category. As we continue to manage our remaining game caps, we are keeping **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Justin Crawford**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros** in reserve to ensure we have the flexibility to chase stolen bases if the leaderboard shifts.",
